==== ARE THE THREE PER-PAIR TDOA ERRORS INDEPENDENT? ====
  (M37) and hence the simple GDOP law (M40) assume Cov(dtau) = sigma_tau^2 I.
  With M = 3 microphones there are only TWO independent delays, and all three
  pairwise correlations are computed from the same three channels, so the
  assumption is suspect. Below: the empirical correlation matrix of the
  per-pair TDOA errors (pairs 1-2, 1-3, 2-3), and the azimuth s.d. predicted
  by the GENERAL expression (M36) with the measured covariance substituted,
  against the simple isotropic form (M40).
  SNR   0 dB  corr(12,13) +0.385  corr(12,23) -0.423  corr(13,23) +0.410
            (M40) isotropic prediction   0.635 deg | (M36) with measured Cov: mean   0.753 deg, range  0.741- 0.766 deg | measured RMSE   0.749 deg
  SNR   5 dB  corr(12,13) +0.435  corr(12,23) -0.330  corr(13,23) +0.390
            (M40) isotropic prediction   0.383 deg | (M36) with measured Cov: mean   0.450 deg, range  0.434- 0.466 deg | measured RMSE   0.456 deg
  SNR  10 dB  corr(12,13) +0.352  corr(12,23) -0.323  corr(13,23) +0.337
